    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0156" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 Chiang Kai-shek/8–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-07T20:00:00+07:00">August 7, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 7—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1302. The Generalissimo informed me this morning (supplementing my telegram No.
                    1272 of August 2, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="81" xml:id="d114-f1"/>) that he expects to
                    be in a position to reply to the suggested revision of the China Theater and
                    SEAC (Southeastern Asia Command) within the next 2 or 3 days.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
